# claude-aws-architect — local consumer settings

> Copy this file to `claude-aws-architect.local.md` (no `.example`) and edit
> the values that apply to this consumer project. The committed `.example`
> file declares every supported field; the local file overrides defaults.

## AWS environment

- **Default region**: TODO (e.g., a single region slug for single-region work).
- **Default account**: TODO (account alias or numeric id; never paste a
  long-lived access key here).
- **Allowed regions**: TODO (list of region slugs the orchestrator may
  reference; out-of-list regions raise an Open Question).
- **Data residency**: TODO (one of the documented residency tiers).

## Cost and budget posture

- **Monthly cost ceiling (USD)**: TODO (orchestrator surfaces a warning when
  a design's ROM exceeds this number).
- **Allow Spot capacity**: TODO (`true` / `false`; default `false` until the
  workload-class table marks the workload as Spot-eligible).
- **Pricing-model preference**: TODO (`on-demand`, `reserved`, `savings-plan`,
  or `evaluate`; default `evaluate`).

## Security posture

- **Read-only AWS API mode**: `true` (default; consumers opt out per request).
- **Wildcard IAM allowed**: `false` (default; only the read-only carveout
  recognised by the IAM rule may relax this).
- **Allow live MCP write-class tool calls**: `false` (default; the
  `aws-api-write-guard` hook blocks write-class calls regardless of this
  flag — this setting is advisory only).

## Observability defaults

- **Default log retention (days)**: TODO.
- **Default tracing**: TODO (e.g., AWS X-Ray active tracing; sampling rule).
- **Required metric namespaces**: TODO (list of namespaces to assert in
  every component contract).

## Spec authoring defaults

- **Default feature slug prefix**: TODO (e.g., a team or product code; left
  empty by default).
- **Required `grounded-by` minimum on `requirements.md`**: TODO (integer ≥ 1;
  default 1).
- **Default per-pillar review status floor**: TODO (`PASS`, `DEFER`, or
  `GAP`; default `PASS` — designs at `GAP` are blocked from advancing past
  `draft`).

## Notes

- Every value above is read by the orchestrator at run time and surfaced in
  the merged output's degraded-signals section if it conflicts with a
  specialist's grounded recommendation.
- Secrets do **not** belong in this file. The `aws-secret-scanner` hook blocks
  any write that contains an AWS access key, session token, private key
  block, or KMS CMK ARN.
